{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>You tested my heart</b> — You know all my thoughts." "And the meaning of <b>at night</b> — in his being alone, away from people." "<b>You will not find</b> — any defect or blemish." "<b>Let not my mouth pass</b> — like \"and waters shall not pass his mouth,\" and behold his thought is in the words of his mouth, and not the reverse."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:24.802928808Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}